# The files of sbase (third_party/sbase, vendored unmodified) that the build
# replaces with ours: the same format and check as musl's
# (user/posix/musl/OVERRIDES, tools/checkoverrides.py). The upstream file
# (relative to third_party/sbase), the SHA-256 of the upstream file ours was
# written against, and our file (relative to the top of the tree). A new
# sbase that changed one of these stops the build until someone has read
# upstream's change, brought ours up to date and recorded the new hash.
#
# Each of these three starts a program with fork + execvp, and Jam OS has no
# fork (docs/M13-PLAN.md question 4): ours is upstream's file with that one
# place made posix_spawnp, failing as the forked child did.

# find -exec / -ok: the command is started by spawn().
find.c c9403764e5dbe67231aca35d61f1240275d2d984f7406a95779951af13dad101 user/ports/sbase/override/find.c
# time: the timed command.
time.c 9e724070b53ff0e3dcf50972057891b93700860ff1985ec2f4b428e400f8c6b9 user/ports/sbase/override/time.c
# xargs: the command, once per batch.
xargs.c cfc0205fc8a87e142bccd73853592680697e1551c8d9e69e2fafc835d62a7ed9 user/ports/sbase/override/xargs.c
